# Machine facts you have seen and accept, for scripts/doctor.sh (never commit your real list).
# Copy to ~/.claude/private/doctor-accepted (or point CLAUDE_DOCTOR_ACCEPTED_FILE at it). One id per line; `#` starts a comment.
# An accepted fact prints as INFO instead of WARN, so the summary's WARN count shows only what needs work. Doctor only reads this file.
# Without the file every WARN stays a WARN. A file that is a link accepts nothing; an id doctor does not know is ignored; either
# gives one WARN. The production host list WARN (no ~/.claude/private/prod-hosts) can never be accepted.
#
# ollama-off            Ollama is not running: recall search is lexical only.
# apple-terminal-notes  Apple Terminal shows no desktop notes (at most a bell).
ollama-off
apple-terminal-notes
